# Application HTML templates

Shared preview/PDF rules live in the **pipeline** (`applicationCatalog` + `injectPaginatedStyles`). Do not invent per-folder page or plot grammar.

## Content tokens

- Survey **inline prose**: prefer `{{PLOT_CS_CTS_NO}}` (kind + number, e.g. `C.T.S. No. 177A`).
- Survey **meta-table row**: key = `Plot No./ C.S. No./ C.T.S. No. / F.P No.` and value = `{{PLOT_NO}} / {{CS_NO}} / {{CTS_NO}} / {{FP_NO}}` — pipeline collapses to key `C.T.S. No.` + value `177A` (plotBelongsTo-aware). Do **not** put `{{PLOT_CS_CTS_NO}}` in the value cell (that repeats the kind label).
- Place **inline prose**: prefer `{{VILLAGE_DIVISION}}` (e.g. `Village KURLA - 4`).
- Place **meta-table row**: key = `Division/ Village/ T.P. Scheme No.` and value = `{{DIVISION}} / {{VILLAGE}} / {{TPS_NO}}` — pipeline collapses to key `Village` + bare place name.
- Application Details **Letter fields** panel: same collapse — one survey field labeled `C.T.S. No.` / `C.S. No.` / `F.P. No.` with the bare number, and one place field labeled `Village` / `Division` / `T.P. Scheme No.` with the bare name. Do not list all four plot tokens and all three place tokens.
- **Letter-field accordions are catalog-driven** — do **not** add per-application accordion code in `application-details/page.tsx`. Set `application_document_placeholders.section_label` (Date / Subject / Reference / Addressee / Proposal / Consultant / Client / Plot / area). Prefer explicit `section_label` for letter-shaped docs. Always set a sensible `placeholders.ui_group` (`subject` / `reference` / `consultant` / `client` / `office` / `other`) so unlabeled docs still group via `sectionTitleFromUiGroup`. Explicit `section_label` always wins over `ui_group`.
- Letter fields: omit empty address line 1/2/3 rows (`owner_address_line_*`, `architect_address_line_*`, `bp_address_line_*`) — only show lines that have a value (same as HTML empty-line cleanup).
- Ward: token value is the **ward code only** (e.g. `L`). Prose may add the word “Ward” once beside the token (`{{WARD}} Ward`). Do not rely on the token appending “Ward”.
- `{{BUILDING_NO}}` / `{{FILE_NO}}` / `{{PROPOSAL_NUMBER}}`: all print Project Details **proposal number** (`project_info.proposalNo`). Supervision / checklist HTML use `{{FILE_NO}}` — catalog must link `file_no` (and plot meta tokens `cts_no` / `plot_no` / …) on those documents; appointment letters historically used `proposal_number` only. Pipeline also hard-fills `{{FILE_NO}}` / `{{BUILDING_NO}}` from proposalNo when empty.
- Consultant letters live under `html/General/consultants/<role>/` as `appointment.html`, `acceptance.html`, `supervision-memo.html`, and `notice-start-of-work.html`. Architect also has `plot-area-certificate.html` (Architect folder only). Owner annexures live under `html/General/owner/` (`plinth-completion.html`, `development-completion-certificate.html`, `owners-plot-area-affidavit.html`, `personal-identification-information.html`). Do **not** use top-level `html/Appointment/` / `html/Acceptance/` or Document Checklist. Catalog paths must match. Supervision / Notice / Architect PAC are on roster-matched `appointment_letter` types; plinth + development completion are on **both** Owner and Architect; Owner's Plot Area Affidavit and Personal Identification Information are Owner-only.
- `{{APPOINTMENT_DATE}}` (supervision memos and any consultant HTML that references appointment): prints the **application created date** (`applications.created_at` → DD/MM/YYYY). Catalog: `appointment_date` computed from `CatalogProjectSource.application_created_at`. Do not leave it blank for users to type unless product adds an override.
- Suburb (`{{SUBURB}}`): derived from project region/ward — **never** hardcode City / Western / Eastern in HTML. Printed value is the region **only** (`City` / `Western` / `Eastern`) — do **not** append “Suburb”. Prefer `save_plot_details.region`; if empty, infer via `inferLocationFromWard(ward)` (same map as Project Details). Used in BMC To-block: `O/o The Dy.Ch.Eng.(B.P.) {{SUBURB}},`
- BMC annexure To-block layout: `To,` alone on its own line, then address lines on the following lines (do not put `To,` beside the first address line). Do **not** print “(On the letter head of …)” notes — letterhead comes from catalog flags / preview chrome only.
- Organisation on BMC annexure To-blocks: hardcode `Brihanmumbai Municipal Corporation` (or resolve `{{BP_ORGANISATION}}` to that literal) — not a free-text project field.
- Building Proposal address lines (Word blanks Address Line 1/2/3): use `{{BP_ADDRESS_LINE_1}}`, `{{BP_ADDRESS_LINE_2}}`, `{{BP_ADDRESS_LINE_3}}` only. Values come from the same Building Proposal office resolution as appointment letters (`resolveBuildingProposalOffice` by region/ward from `building_proposal_offices`). Do **not** hardcode office street addresses in HTML.
- Label/value meta rows (`.meta-table`): keep keys and values **close** — label column shrink-wraps (`width:1%; white-space:nowrap; padding-right:~10px`), not a wide fixed % that leaves a large gap. Values stay left-aligned in the second column and wrap under themselves.
- `Subject:` / `Reference:` side headings are **normal weight**; bold only the value (e.g. Acceptance of Supervision, file no.) — same as Word annexures.
- Closing blocks: wrap `Thanking you` / `Yours Faithfully` + signature in `.closing`; signature details in `.sig`; CC in `.cc` (letters may use `.cc-box`). Letterheaded checklist forms must **not** set `break-inside`/`break-before: avoid` on those wrappers (Paged.js drops the body).
- **`C.C. to:` is static chrome** — use `<span class="cc-label">C.C. to:</span>` (normal weight, same as appointment letters). Never wrap `C.C. to:` in `.value-bold` or `.bold`. Do not treat it as a catalog Letter field.
- C.C. / owner role: use `{{OWNER_OR_DEVELOPER}}` (resolves to **Owner** or **Developer** from the roster). Never hardcode `Owner/Developer`. On the C.C. line, print the role as plain/`.bold` prose — **not** `.value-bold`. Name / firm / address lines under C.C. stay `.value-bold`.
- Supervision memo C.C. (Structural / Plumber / Site Supervisor): **no** `1.` / `2.` numbering. Blocks are:
  - `C.C. to:` → `{{OWNER_OR_DEVELOPER}}` + owner name/firm/address
  - then Architect/L.S. **labeled** block (same as signer) — never the combined phrase “Architect/ Licensed Surveyor”
- Architect / L.S. role from project roster only: `{{ARCHITECT_OR_LS_ROLE}}` → **Architect** or **Licensed Surveyor** (whichever is on the project). Reg side-heading: `{{ARCHITECT_OR_LS_REG_LABEL}}` → `COA Reg. No.` (Architect) or `Reg. No.` (L.S.).
- Architect C.C. / signer labeled block (always this shape):
  ```
  {{ARCHITECT_OR_LS_ROLE}}
  Name: {{ARCHITECT_LS_NAME}}
  {{ARCHITECT_OR_LS_REG_LABEL}}: {{ARCHITECT_LS_REG_NO}}
  Valid upto: {{ARCHITECT_LS_VALIDITY}}
  Date: {{LETTER_DATE}}
  ```
  Resolve these from the **Architect / L.S. roster row** in `applicationCatalog` (not the memo signer). Other consultants keep their role title + `Reg. No.:`. Do not print bare `{{SALUTATION}}{{NAME}},` / bare reg / bare validity stacks.
- DSC space: add `<div class="dsc-stamp-slot" aria-hidden="true"></div>` **only** where catalog `sign` requires a digital signature — not on every block.
  - Size/air must match appointment letters: **180×60** with **8px** margin above and below (same as `html/_shared/application-templates.css` → `.signature-table .dsc-stamp-slot`). Do not shrink this pocket on forms — DSC placement depends on it.
  - `sign` includes `owner` → `dsc-stamp-slot dsc-stamp-slot--owner` above the owner name lines.
  - `sign` includes `architect_or_ls` or `consultant` → `dsc-stamp-slot` after `For {{CONSULTANT_FIRM}},` and before the signer name.
  - Skip DSC slots when `sign` is empty / document is not DSC-signed.
- Letterhead: catalog `show_letterhead` / `letterhead_source` only — do not paint letterhead images in HTML. Pipeline uses the **assigned person’s** letterhead only (no owner↔consultant fallback). If that person has no letterhead image, still **reserve** the logo/footer band when `show_letterhead` (blank space) — do not collapse chrome.
- First line under letterhead (`ANNEXURE …` / form title): do **not** add HTML top padding or blank spacer blocks. When `show_letterhead`, pipeline matches appointment/acceptance clearance (115pt first-page top), with or without an image. Same rule for every letterheaded annexure / supervision HTML.
- Equal body font: body + meta labels/values at **10.5pt**. Do **not** shrink CTS/meta values to 9pt for page-1 fit. Form title may stay **11.5pt** as a heading.
- Page-1 fit (every letterheaded form): match pipeline densify — line-height ~**1.05–1.06**, near-zero vertical margins on `p` / `.to-block` / `.meta-table` / `.closing` / `.cc`. DSC pocket stays **180×60**; outer margin may be **2px**. Do not invent per-folder densify CSS.
- Narrative paragraphs: first-line tab **0.5in** — forms use class `body-indent`; appointment uses `p.opening`; acceptance uses `.eeb-tab-line.opening` / `.acceptance-body`. Do **not** indent Subject, Reference, Dear Sir / Sir, To-block, Thanking you / `.closing-line`, signer blocks, or C.C. Shared CSS + pipeline must not force `text-indent: 0` on those narrative classes.
- Pagination: rely on `injectPaginatedStyles`; do not add one-off `@page` / min-height page hacks per folder.

## After HTML changes

Upload with:

```bash
node scripts/sync-application-templates.mjs --dir "./html/General/consultants"
node scripts/sync-application-templates.mjs --dir "./html/General/document checklist"
# or specific paths matching application_documents.html
```

Object keys must match the catalog `html` column (paths relative to `html/`).
